<article class="env-proposition" id="05BX">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05BX">Proposition <span data-tag="05BX">4.8.6.12</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer and let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an $n$-categorical inner fibration of $\infty $-categories. Then $F$ is $(n+1)$-faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof of Proposition <a data-tag="05BX" href="/tag/05BX">4.8.6.12</a>.</strong>
       If $n \leq -2$, then $F$ is an isomorphism of simplicial sets and therefore an equivalence of $\infty $-categories (Example <a data-tag="01E0" href="/tag/01E0">4.5.1.11</a>). If $n = -1$, then $F$ is an isomorphism from $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ onto a full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, and therefore fully faithful (Example <a data-tag="01JJ" href="/tag/01JJ">4.8.3.2</a>). We may therefore assume without loss of generality that $n \geq 0$. By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="05BD" href="/tag/05BD">4.8.3.36</a>, we may assume without loss of generality that $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is a standard simplex; in this case, we wish to show that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is locally $(n-1)$-truncated. This follows from Warning <a data-tag="0580" href="/tag/0580">4.7.7.21</a>, since $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an $n$-category (Proposition <a data-tag="05BU" href="/tag/05BU">4.8.6.9</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
